VALUES ('e2c1bbaa-8037-4070-a167-657636853df6', '618cd3c1-3524-40e3-a516-9c499d476e97', 'CLINICAL_CASE', 2, '{"scenario":"A 28-year-old motor vehicle crash victim arrives in the trauma bay with severe midfacial trauma. On examination, there is extensive periorbital ecchymosis, a flattened ","question":"Which of the following maxillofacial fractures is present in this patient?","explanation":"A Le Fort III fracture (Craniofacial Dysjunction) separates the entire facial skeleton from the cranial base via fractures through the nasofrontal suture, ethmoid cribriform plate, superior orbital fissure, lateral orbital wall, and zygomaticofrontal suture. The clinical hallmarks present here are the classic "}'::jsonb)
