VALUES ('816f19a3-9491-46f8-a81c-95dd9d032b14', '953c70ae-753c-4c96-ab28-61146c546f2e', 'CLINICAL_CASE', 2, '{"scenario":"A 2-day-old male infant born to a diabetic mother develops profound cyanosis that fails to improve despite administration of 100% oxygen via a non-rebreather mask (hyperoxia challenge test shows PaO2 42 mmHg). Vital signs: RR 68/min, HR 158 bpm, SpO2 64%. Physical examination demonstrates central cyanosis without a significant heart murmur. Chest radiograph demonstrates mild cardiomegaly with a narrow mediastinum, resembling an ","question":"Which of the following represents the underlying embryological defect and the immediate life-saving medical intervention?","explanation":"This newborn presents with refractory cyanosis (unresponsive to 100% oxygen) and an "}'::jsonb)
